---

import { env } from 'cloudflare:workers'
const isProduction = env.PUBLIC_IS_PRODUCTION
---
<script is:inline set:html={`window.__isProduction = ${isProduction}`}/>

{/*
  `capture_exceptions: true` because this shop's traffic arrives through
  in-app browsers — Instagram's above all — which expose no console and accept
  no debugger. An error there is invisible unless the page reports it, and the
  first checkout bug those browsers produced had to be diagnosed blind. `true`
  enables the default set: unhandled errors and unhandled promise rejections,
  which is exactly the shape of a page script dying at load. Set in code
  rather than left to the project's remote setting, so what is captured does
  not depend on a dashboard toggle.

  ONE KNOWN GAP: the handlers install when the async `array.js` arrives, so an
  error that fires before it on a cold cache is missed. Absence of a captured
  exception is therefore not absence of an error.

  `posthog.init` LIVES INSIDE THE GUARD. It sat after it, where every
  non-production stage — which never defines the `posthog` stub — threw a
  ReferenceError on load.
*/}
